   8    512      8.00 |   18812.9   0.823 |     522.7   385.2 |   18895.3   116.4    0.842   0.4% | -
  16    256      4.00 |   19029.3   0.814 |     530.2   379.8 |   19131.8   114.9    0.807   0.5% | -
  32    128      2.00 |   38013.2   0.407 |     644.2   312.5 |   38176.6    57.6    0.746   0.4% | -

seg_eff = t_full/t_seg (segmentation-only GEMM efficiency).
ovl_eff = (t_seg + t_comm - t_ovl) / min(t_seg, t_comm); 1.0 means the
shorter phase is fully hidden. bub% = t_ovl over max(t_seg, t_comm).
The sweet spot is the S with the lowest t_ovl: finer chunks start compute
earlier but pay tile quantization + per-chunk signalling; coarser chunks
expose the first chunk's flight time.
